{"description": "Asks a RAG collection one or more questions and outputs the matching chunks as a ranked table with their source location and corpus version - the same retrieval a deployed decision performs.", "displayName": "RAG - Retrieve Context.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [{"name": "_rgrt_questionTable", "displayName": "_rgrt_questionTable", "minEntries": 0, "maxEntries": 1, "type": "table", "id": "_rgrt_questionTable", "label": "_rgrt_questionTable"}], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgrt_results", "displayName": "_rgrt_results", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - Retrieve Context.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - Retrieve Context: ask a RAG collection one or more questions and\n * output the matching chunks as a table - the same retrieval the manifested\n * model performs for a decision, landing somewhere it can be read, compared\n * and turned into an evaluation set. Read-only: it never writes to the\n * collection or the ledger. Thin shell over rag_core.steps.run_retrieve -\n * see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgrt_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgrt_ragProject) %then %global _rgrt_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgrt_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgrt_tablesCaslib;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgrt_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgrt_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n%mend _rgrt_setup;\n%_rgrt_setup;\n/* Pipeline-wide state, shared by every RAG step in this session.\n   RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR: 1 (default) stops a SAS Studio Flow at the failing\n   step, which is what an interactive user wants. A SCHEDULED run sets it to\n   0: an aborted session never sends SAS Job Execution its completion\n   handshake, so the job would report running forever and its dead compute\n   server would keep counting against the context's server limit.\n   RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED: set by the step that fails; later steps then skip\n   their work and pass the inventory through, so the flow finishes tidily\n   instead of loading half a corpus. */\n%macro _rag_pipeline_state;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR) %then %do;\n        %global RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR;\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED) %then %global RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rag_pipeline_state;\n%_rag_pipeline_state;\n\n%let _rgrt_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgrt_rc = 1;\n%let _rgrt_state = run;\n%let _rgrt_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgrt_summary = ;\n%let _rgrt_nrows = 0;\n\n%macro _rgrt_guard;\n    %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rgrt_guard;\n%_rgrt_guard;\n%macro _rgrt_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgrt_results) %then %global _rgrt_results;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgrt_results)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgrt_results = rgrtout.&_rgrt_ragProject._RETRIEVAL;\n%mend _rgrt_port_default;\n%_rgrt_port_default;\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rgrtout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rgrtcas uuidmac=_rgrt_casuuid;\n%let _rgrt_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgrt_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rgrtout cas caslib=\"&_rgrt_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rgrtcas;\n\n%macro _rgrt_export(portvar, file);\n    %if %symexist(&portvar.) %then %do;\n        %if %length(%superq(&&portvar.)) GT 0 %then %do;\n            %if %sysfunc(exist(&&&portvar..)) %then %do;\n                filename _rgrt_io \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/&file.\";\n                proc json out=_rgrt_io noSASTags;\n                    export &&&portvar..;\n                run; quit;\n                filename _rgrt_io clear;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgrt_export;\n%_rgrt_export(_rgrt_questionTable, rgrt_questions_in.json);\n\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    # nothing to do when the step is only passing the inventory through\n    if str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrt_state\") or \"run\").strip() != \"run\":\n        return\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGRETRIEVE \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrt_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrt_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrt_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgrt_backend\",\n        \"_rgrt_collection\",\n        \"_rgrt_storeHost\",\n        \"_rgrt_storePort\",\n        \"_rgrt_storeDb\",\n        \"_rgrt_storeSslmode\",\n        \"_rgrt_storeSsl\",\n        \"_rgrt_credentialDomain\",\n        \"_rgrt_questions\",\n        \"_rgrt_topK\",\n        \"_rgrt_filterJson\",\n        \"_rgrt_scrEndpoint\",\n        \"_rgrt_embedModel\",\n        \"_rgrt_deploymentType\",\n        \"_rgrt_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgrt_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgrt_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def multiline(control):\n        \"\"\"Every line a user typed into a multi-line text field.\n\n        SAS Studio splits such a field for us: it emits <control>_count and\n        <control>_1..N, and leaves the plain macro variable holding only the\n        FIRST line. Reading just the plain one silently turned two questions\n        into one run-on question (found live in a flow). Semicolons are still\n        accepted, for callers that set the parameter directly.\n        \"\"\"\n        values = []\n        try:\n            count = int(float(SAS.symget(control + \"_count\") or 0))\n        except Exception:\n            count = 0\n        if count > 0:\n            for index in range(1, count + 1):\n                try:\n                    piece = str(SAS.symget(\"%s_%d\" % (control, index)) or \"\")\n                except Exception:\n                    piece = \"\"\n                if piece.strip():\n                    values.append(piece.strip())\n            if values:\n                return values\n        raw = str(P.get(control) or \"\").replace(\";\", \"\\n\")\n        return [line.strip() for line in raw.split(\"\\n\") if line.strip()]\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        try:\n            conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrt_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                            port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgrt_casport\") or 5570)),\n                            password=TOKEN,\n                            session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrt_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # The step reuses the CAS session SAS created, because the staged\n            # table has to be visible to the casutil promote that follows. CAS\n            # only lets an identity reconnect to its OWN session, and a context\n            # that runs the server as a service account breaks that: SAS and\n            # its token are the service account while the CAS session belongs\n            # to the user who launched the job.\n            #\n            # SWAT's exception says only \"Could not connect ... on port 5570\";\n            # the server's real message (\"Users can only reconnect to their own\n            # sessions\") goes to stderr and never reaches the exception, so\n            # matching on text does not work. Connecting WITHOUT the session id\n            # separates the two causes: if that works, CAS is reachable and the\n            # problem is whose session it is.\n            reachable = False\n            try:\n                probe = swat.CAS(\n                    hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrt_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                    port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgrt_casport\") or 5570)),\n                    password=TOKEN)\n                reachable = True\n                probe.close()\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            if reachable:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    \"this compute context cannot run the RAG steps: CAS is \"\n                    \"reachable, but the SAS session and the CAS session belong \"\n                    \"to different identities, so the step cannot reuse the CAS \"\n                    \"session it needs. The stock 'SAS Job Execution compute \"\n                    \"context' has this problem because it runs the server as a \"\n                    \"service account. Run the job in a context that runs as the \"\n                    \"REQUESTING USER - the 'SAS Studio compute context' does, \"\n                    \"and a full flow was verified there. See the RAG \"\n                    \"administration guide.\")\n            raise\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgrt_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgrt_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgrt_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgrt_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgrt_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        from rag_core.adapters import get_adapter\n        from rag_core.credentials import fetch_secrets, store_config_from_secrets\n        from rag_core.scr import EmbeddingClient\n        from rag_core.steps import RETRIEVE_COLUMNS, run_retrieve\n\n        missing = [name for name in (\"collection\", \"storeHost\", \"storeDb\")\n                   if not P[\"_rgrt_\" + name]]\n        if missing:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"required parameters missing: \"\n                               + \", \".join(missing))\n\n        # questions come from a wired table, a typed list, or both\n        questions = []\n        listed = WORKPATH + \"rgrt_questions_in.json\"\n        if os.path.exists(listed):\n            for row in read_rows(\"rgrt_questions_in.json\", \"\"):\n                for column in (\"question\", \"text\", \"prompt\", \"query\"):\n                    if row.get(column):\n                        questions.append(str(row[column]))\n                        break\n        questions.extend(multiline(\"_rgrt_questions\"))\n        if not questions:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"nothing to ask - type a question, or wire a \"\n                               \"table with a question column into this step\")\n\n        filters = None\n        if str(P[\"_rgrt_filterJson\"] or \"\").strip():\n            filters = json.loads(P[\"_rgrt_filterJson\"])\n\n        domain = P[\"_rgrt_credentialDomain\"] or \"agentic-ai-keys\"\n        secrets = fetch_secrets(BASE, TOKEN, domain, verify=VERIFY)\n        if not secrets:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"no credential resolved from domain \" + domain\n                               + \" for this user - see the Managing \"\n                               \"Credentials administration guide\")\n        backend = P[\"_rgrt_backend\"] or \"pgvector\"\n        sslmode = (P[\"_rgrt_storeSslmode\"] if backend == \"pgvector\"\n                   else P[\"_rgrt_storeSsl\"])\n        adapter = get_adapter(backend)\n        adapter.connect(store_config_from_secrets(\n            secrets, backend, P[\"_rgrt_storeHost\"], P[\"_rgrt_storePort\"],\n            P[\"_rgrt_storeDb\"], sslmode))\n\n        # the query side of the SAME embedding model the corpus was built\n        # with - a different model puts the question in a different space\n        client = EmbeddingClient(\n            P[\"_rgrt_scrEndpoint\"] or (BASE + \"/llm\"),\n            P[\"_rgrt_embedModel\"] or \"all_minilm_l6_v2\",\n            deployment_type=P[\"_rgrt_deploymentType\"] or \"k8s\",\n            verify_ssl=VERIFY)\n        collection = P[\"_rgrt_collection\"]\n        top_k = int(float(P[\"_rgrt_topK\"] or 4)) or 4\n        rows = run_retrieve(questions, client, adapter, collection,\n                            k=top_k, filter=filters, log=M)\n        adapter.close()\n\n        n_rows = write_rows(\"rgrt_results_out.json\", rows, RETRIEVE_COLUMNS,\n                            numeric=(\"rank\", \"page\", \"span_start\", \"span_end\",\n                                     \"distance\", \"score\"))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrt_nrows\", str(n_rows))\n\n        answered = len(set(r[\"question\"] for r in rows if r[\"rank\"] > 0))\n        failed = len(set(r[\"question\"] for r in rows\n                         if r[\"rank\"] == 0 and r[\"error_text\"]\n                         and \"no chunks\" not in r[\"error_text\"]))\n        summarize(\"collection \" + collection + \" on \" + backend\n                  + \", top \" + str(top_k))\n        summarize(\"embedding model \" + (P[\"_rgrt_embedModel\"]\n                                        or \"all_minilm_l6_v2\") + \" (query mode)\")\n        summarize(str(len(set(r[\"question\"] for r in rows))) + \" questions asked, \"\n                  + str(answered) + \" returned chunks\"\n                  + (\", \" + str(failed) + \" failed\" if failed else \"\"))\n        if filters:\n            summarize(\"filter applied: \" + json.dumps(filters)[:120])\n        summarize(str(n_rows) + \" result rows written\")\n        publish_summary(\"_rgrt_summary\")\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrt_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrt_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgrt_emit_results;\n    %if &_rgrt_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgrt_results., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgrt_results., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgrtout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgrtcas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgrt_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgrt_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgrt_nrows. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgrtreo \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgrt_results_out.json\";\n        libname rgrtrej json fileref=rgrtreo;\n        data &_rgrt_results.&opts.;\n            length question $ 1000 doc_id $ 40 chunk_id $ 64 filename $ 256\n                      source_uri $ 1024 heading_path $ 512\n                      ingestion_timestamp $ 32 corpus_run_id $ 32\n                      content $ 8000 error_text $ 500;\n            label question=\"Question\" rank=\"Rank (1 = closest)\" doc_id=\"Document ID\"\n                  chunk_id=\"Chunk ID\" filename=\"Source file\"\n                  source_uri=\"Source location\" heading_path=\"Heading path\"\n                  page=\"Page number\" span_start=\"Start offset in document\"\n                  span_end=\"End offset in document\"\n                  ingestion_timestamp=\"Chunk ingested (UTC)\"\n                  corpus_run_id=\"Corpus version (ingestion run)\"\n                  distance=\"Distance (lower = closer)\" score=\"Score (higher = better)\"\n                  content=\"Chunk text\" error_text=\"Failure reason\";\n            set rgrtrej.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgrtrej clear;\n        filename rgrtreo clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgrt_results.&opts.;\n            length question $ 1000 doc_id $ 40 chunk_id $ 64 filename $ 256\n                      source_uri $ 1024 heading_path $ 512\n                      ingestion_timestamp $ 32 corpus_run_id $ 32\n                      content $ 8000 error_text $ 500;\n            label question=\"Question\" rank=\"Rank (1 = closest)\" doc_id=\"Document ID\"\n                  chunk_id=\"Chunk ID\" filename=\"Source file\"\n                  source_uri=\"Source location\" heading_path=\"Heading path\"\n                  page=\"Page number\" span_start=\"Start offset in document\"\n                  span_end=\"End offset in document\"\n                  ingestion_timestamp=\"Chunk ingested (UTC)\"\n                  corpus_run_id=\"Corpus version (ingestion run)\"\n                  distance=\"Distance (lower = closer)\" score=\"Score (higher = better)\"\n                  content=\"Chunk text\" error_text=\"Failure reason\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgrt_emit_results;\n%_rgrt_emit_results;\n\nlibname rgrtout clear;\ncas rgrtcas terminate;\n\n%macro _rgrt_status;\n    %if &_rgrt_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgrt_rc. NE 0 %then\n        %let _rgrt_state = fail;\n    %if &_rgrt_state. EQ skip %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Retrieve Context: skipped -----\";\n        run;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgrt_state. EQ fail %then %do;\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 1;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"ERROR: RAG - Retrieve Context failed: %superq(_rgrt_error)\";\n        run;\n        %if &RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR. NE 0 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                abort 42;\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    data _null_;\n        length part $ 500;\n        putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Retrieve Context -----\";\n        do i = 1 to countw(\"%superq(_rgrt_summary)\", \"|\");\n            part = strip(scan(\"%superq(_rgrt_summary)\", i, \"|\"));\n            if part ne \"\" then putLog \"NOTE:   \" part;\n        end;\n    run;\n%mend _rgrt_status;\n%_rgrt_status;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Asks a RAG collection one or more questions and returns the matching chunks as a table, ranked, with the source location and corpus version of each. This is the same retrieval a deployed decision performs - useful for checking what a collection actually answers, comparing configurations, or building an evaluation set. It never writes to the collection or the ledger.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_questions\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Question (one per line, or separated by semicolons):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"e.g. How long can a flight be for economy class?\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_questionTable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"inputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"...or a table of questions (question / text / prompt / query column):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_ragProject\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"RAG project (names the output table):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_collection\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Collection to search:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_topK\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"numstepper\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Chunks to return per question:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"integer\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"min\": 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"max\": 100,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"stepsize\": 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_storeHost\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store host:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_storeDb\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Database name:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"pgvector\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"pgvector (PostgreSQL)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"singlestore\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SingleStore\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_storePort\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store port (blank = the backend default: 5432 pgvector, 3306 singlestore):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_storeSslmode\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SSL mode:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"disable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"disable\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"allow\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"allow\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"prefer\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"prefer\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"require\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"verify-ca\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"verify-ca\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"verify-full\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"verify-full\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgrt_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pgvector\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_storeSsl\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"TLS:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"require (TLS)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"disable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"disable (no TLS)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgrt_backend\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"singlestore\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_filterJson\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Metadata filter (JSON, e.g. {\\\"doc_id\\\": \\\"...\\\"}):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_embedModel\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Embedding model (must be the one the corpus was built with):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_scrEndpoint\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SCR base URL of the embedding container (blank = this deployment's /llm):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_deploymentType\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SCR deployment type:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"k8s\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Kubernetes\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"aca\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Azure Container Apps\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_tablesCaslib\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Caslib for the results table:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_credentialDomain\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Credential domain:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgrt_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrt_results\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Retrieval results output:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - Retrieve Context step\\n==========\\n\\nRuns real retrieval against a collection and writes the results to a table: one row per matching chunk, carrying rank, distance and score alongside the source file, heading, page and character span, and the corpus run that produced the chunk. Questions come from the field, from a wired table, or both. The question is embedded through the SAME SCR model the corpus was built with, in query mode - a different model would place the question in a different vector space and quietly return nonsense. Only LIVE chunks are searched: retired generations stay in the collection for point-in-time reads but never surface here. A question that fails to embed or search reports on its own row and the others still run; a question that matches nothing gets a rank-0 row, so it is visible rather than absent.\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents \u2192 Extract Text \u2192 Chunk Documents \u2192 Embed Chunks \u2192 Load Vector Store. The bulk data travels beside the flow in promoted CAS tables named <project>_ELEMENTS, <project>_CHUNKS, <project>_EMBEDDED and <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib (each saved to disk, so state survives server restarts; names stay within 32 characters so they display nicely in SAS Studio). Each step's output table lands in that same caslib as <project>_INV_LIST, _INV_EXTRACT, _INV_CHUNK, _INV_EMBED and <project>_LOAD_REPORT unless you point the output port somewhere else. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages (swat/pandas carry the pipeline tables to CAS - varchar columns, no 32k limit).\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\\n* psycopg2-binary for the pgvector (PostgreSQL) backend.\\n* singlestoredb for the SingleStore backend.\\n* A credential domain (default agentic-ai-keys) holding <BACKEND>_RAG_USER/<BACKEND>_RAG_PW entries.\\n* The embedding model published as an SCR container, reachable from this compute context.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Documentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Read-only: this step never writes to the collection or the ledger, so it is safe to run against a live corpus while ingestion is happening - it takes no run lock.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.2 (29JUL2026)\\n      - SAS Content document sources; output tables land in the tables caslib; labelled columns; numeric and list-of-values fields; run summary in the log\\n* Version: 1.1 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Pipeline tables move to promoted CAS tables via SWAT (varchar, no 32k limit); automatic embed checkpoint\\n* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgrt_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_ragProject\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_tablesCaslib\": \"casuser\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_collection\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_questions\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_topK\": 4,\n\t\t\"_rgrt_storeHost\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_storePort\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_storeDb\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_filterJson\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_embedModel\": \"all_minilm_l6_v2\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_scrEndpoint\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrt_deploymentType\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"k8s\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Kubernetes\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgrt_backend\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"pgvector\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"pgvector (PostgreSQL)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgrt_storeSslmode\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"prefer\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"prefer\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgrt_storeSsl\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"require (TLS)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgrt_credentialDomain\": \"agentic-ai-keys\"\n\t}\n}"}